{
  "_comment": "Cross-language parity fixture for the credential-SHAPE vocabulary SSOT. Consumed by runners that MUST agree: (Python) tests/test_credential_shapes_parity.py against vco_lib.credential_shapes; (bash) templates/hooks/_lib/credshapes.sh; (PowerShell) templates/hooks/_lib/credshapes.ps1; (bash) tools/vct-secrets/lib/credential_shapes.sh for the argv_name rows. Python is the SSOT (A>B>C); this fixture locks every mirror to it. A divergence in any mirror fails that language's parity leg. EVERY value here is SYNTHETIC and built from character repeats so a miscount cannot silently weaken a case and no real-looking token literal enters the repo. The sk-or-v1- tails are 40 chars, not OpenRouter's canonical 64: GitHub push protection pattern-matches the full canonical length in file content, while the sk_vendor_key shape needs only an unbroken >=32 tail — 40 satisfies our scanner and stays inert to theirs. AKIAIOSFODNN7EXAMPLE is AWS's own published documentation key.",
  "_note": "Each case: name; text (the haystack); context (repo_scan|content_scan|command_scan|argv_name); expect_ids (the shape ids that MUST match, in SSOT declaration order; [] means the input must NOT be flagged in that context). The excalidraw_locale_* rows pin the still-live false-positive corpus: the Slovak locale chunk name in the vendored Excalidraw bundle must never be flagged. The *_repo_absent rows pin the deliberate omission of base64-collision-prone shapes from repo_scan. Optional `path` on a case: the scanned file, so shapes restricted to another file kind are dropped (patterns_for_file / credshapes_for_context CONTEXT PATH / Get-CredShapes -Path). `file_kinds` pins file_kind(path) in every leg (owner ruling 2026-10-13: unquoted values are literals only in env/config-style files).",
  "_format_version": 1,
